    "summary": "`backlog_check` returned no blocking issues, only one warning: 46 items carry open questions, and they are listed in the backlog's open-questions section. Every FR-001 to FR-033 and NFR-001 to NFR-011 in prd.md maps to at least one story. Release 1 holds FR-001..005, 007..024, 027, 028, 030 and 031, and Release 2 holds FR-006, 025, 026, 029, 032 and 033. That matches the request and the DL-1 and DL-2 deadlines. I read the backlog.md detail only through E-002, plus the Open questions and Release 2 closing sections. I confirmed the rest of the coverage from the coverage map, the release descriptions and spot checks of the JSON. The acceptance criteria I read are testable, with measures such as 10 minutes, 5 tries, 15 minutes, 7 days, 30 minutes idle and a p95 of 2 s. Migration tasks are not AI-eligible. The one AI-eligible auth-tagged task is the access-docs task (001-T050).\n\nWarnings a human can accept:\n- The 24-month and 90-day retention figures and the manager erasure screen (E-001 US6/US7) are not in the PRD's functional requirements. They come from architecture ASM-012 and ASM-013, and the backlog flags this and suggests they could be cut.\n- The agent flags every estimate-versus-scope/estimate.md gap in the open questions. Release 1 is about 2x the Phase 2 estimate, and Release 2 as requested is not covered by it. The reviewer needs to re-baseline or cut scope before DL-1 is committed.\n- Open product questions are stated rather than decided: Q-007, Q-008, Q-009, Q-015, the client's agreement to the SMS fallback, and STOP replies via SMS only.\n- Migration file names and numbers collide across features, for example 0003_identity_sessions in feature 001 and 0003_online_booking in feature 003, and 002 uses `<rev>`. The backlog notes that migration order needs agreeing, so this should be settled at implementation time.\n- File paths for features 003 to 005 are marked as to be confirmed against merged code."
